          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+object"} ring object
            from it in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            is the corresponding “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+ring"}> group ring
            ” construction generalized to homotopy theory.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p One may consider the construction at various levels of algebraic structure:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
                and
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+fields"} ground fields
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#ChainsOnLoopSpaces"} Chains on loop spaces
            %li
              %p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groups"} ∞-groups
                and
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InfinityGroupInfintyRings"} ∞-Group E-∞ rings
            %li
              %p
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-groups"} H-groups
                and
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#HGroupRingSpectra"} H-group ring spectra
          %h3#ChainsOnLoopSpaces Chains on loop spaces
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            is equivalently (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+space"} based loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "looping#ForTopologicalSpacesAndInfinityGroupoids"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(\Omega X)
            of loop space models the spectrum
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H k(\Omega X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H k
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
          %p
            This
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(\Omega X)
            generallu inherits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"} A-infinity algebra
            structure (
            %a{:href => "#Stasheff1963"}> Stasheff 1963 Thm. 2.3
            ).
          %p
            If the loop space is equivalently modeled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+loops"} Moore loops
            and as such becomes a strict
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+monoid"} topological monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Moore
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(\Omega_{Moore} X)
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Rivera22"} Rivera 2022
          %h3#InfinityGroupInfintyRings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Group
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          #GroupOfUnitsFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi gl
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi AbGrp
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    gl_1 \; \colon \;  CRing_\infty \to AbGrp_\infty
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} commutative ∞-ring
              to its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+of+units"} ∞-group of units
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+of+units"} ∞-group of units
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupOfUnitsFunctor"}
              is a right-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mn ∞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi gl
                            %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mi AbGrp
                      %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CRing_\infty
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\mathbb{S}[-]}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{gl_1}{\to}}
                    AbGrp_\infty
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#ABGHR08"}> ABGHR 08, theorem 2.1/3.2, remark 3.4
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi AbGrp
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi CRing
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}[-] \colon AbGrp_\infty \to CRing_\infty
            %p
              is a higher analog of forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+ring"} group ring
              of an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo →
                    %mi CRing
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{Z}[-] \colon Ab \to CRing
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is indeed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to forming the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
              of a ring.
            %p
              We might call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[A]
              the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-ring"} ∞-group ∞-ring
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
          %h3#HGroupRingSpectra H-Group ring spectra
          %p
            We consider here the simpler concept after passage to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
          %p Recall
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top), \times, \ast)
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with respect to forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+spaces"} product spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            is the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point space
          %p
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
            version
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top^{\ast/}), \wedge, S^0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            is the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Spectra), \wedge, \mathbb{S})
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            is the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho(Top^{\ast/})
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{U}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  Ho(Top)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_+
            adjoins basepoint. This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "pointed+object#WedgeAndSmashOfBasePointAdjoinedTopologicalSpaces"} this example
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X \times Y)_+ \simeq X_+ \wedge Y_+
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then there is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn ∞
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho(Spectra)
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{\Omega^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{\Sigma^\infty}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {}
                  Ho(Top^{\ast/})
          %p
            (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableHomotopyCategoryIsIndeedStabilizationOfClassicalHomotopyCategory"} this prop.
          %p
            Again the left adjoint is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            in that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma^\infty( (X,x) \wedge (Y,y) )
                  \\simeq
                  \\left(\Sigma^\infty (X,x)\right)
                  \\wedge
                  \\left(
                  \\Sigma^\infty (Y,y)
                  \\right)
          %p
            (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#SuspensionSpectrumStructuredStrictQuillenAdjunction"} this prop
          %p Accordingly also the composite functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S}[-] \coloneqq \Sigma^\infty(-)_+
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn ∞
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn ∞
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho(Spectra)
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{\Omega^\infty}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{\Sigma^\infty}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {}
                  Ho(Top^{\ast/})
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{U}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{(-)_+}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  Ho(Top)
          %p are strong monoidal.
          %p
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[-] = \Sigma^\infty((-)_+)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mu)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top), \times , \ast)
            (an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-space"} H-space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma^\infty (A_+)
                  \\;\in\;
                  Ho(Spectra)
          %p
            is a monoid. This is the “monoid ring spectrum” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = G
            is in fact a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(Top),\times, \ast)
            (hence an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma^\infty(G_+)
                  \\;\in \;
                  Ho(Spectra)
          %p
            the
            %em H-group ring spectrum
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          #HGroupRingSpectrumSplitsAsDirectSumWithSphereSpectrum.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (H-group ring spectrum is a direct sum with the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %p
              Notice that an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              already is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              itself, pointed by its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon \ast \to G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G,e) \in Ho(Top^{\ast/})
              this way then the pointed object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_+
              above is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∨
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_+ \simeq (G,e) \vee S^0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Σ
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi Σ
                              %mn ∞
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi G
                              %mo ,
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ∨
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 0
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi G
                              %mo ,
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mo ∨
                            %mi 𝕊
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi G
                              %mo ,
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Sigma^\infty(G_+)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\Sigma^\infty
                    \\left(
                    (G,e)
                    \\vee
                    S^0
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\left( \Sigma^\infty(G,e)  \right) \vee \mathbb{S}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\left( \Sigma^\infty(G,e)  \right) \oplus \mathbb{S}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              (where the last isomorphism exhibits that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
              (by
              = succeed "))." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableHomotopyCategoryHasCoproducts"} this lemma
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The localization of the
              = succeed "-group" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi BU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty(BU(1)_+)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
              at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+element"} Bott element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
              of complex
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi β
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi KU
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}[B U(1)][\beta^{-1}]  \simeq KU
            %p
              This is
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snaith%27s+theorem"} Snaith's theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
              \-algebra
            structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+space"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
              \-space
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Stasheff1963
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              , Thm. 2.3 of:
              %em Homotopy associativity of H-spaces II
              %strong 108
              2 (1963) 293-312 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1993609"}> doi:10.2307/1993609
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0158400-5"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1963-0158400-5
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigidification+of+quasi-categories"} rigidified
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+monoid"} topological monoid
            by using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+loops"} Moore loops
            then the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            stucture. As such this is discussed in relation to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobar+construction"} cobar construction
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Frank+Adams"}> John Frank Adams
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the cobar construction
                %strong 42
                7 (1956) 409–412 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073%2Fpnas.42.7.409"}> doi:10.1073/pnas.42.7.409
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camilo+Arias+Abad"}> Camilo Arias Abad
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Florian+Sch%C3%A4tz"} Florian Schätz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Flat
                    = succeed "-graded" do
